{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Epic 7e9e: BLOCK x2 CRITICAL. E2 — criterion 6 promised 'parametrized tests over the rejected set' without enumerating it; now names the five header names and CR/LF/NUL explicitly. T8 — REAL DESIGN GAP: no fallback specified for an absent ${run:...} substituend. Verified only two production gate_config scopes exist (gate_dispatch:167, :762); code-review, named as a gate op in the epic's own Context, opens none and has no ticket, so ${run:trace_id}/${run:ticket_id} are absent there. Decided: omit the whole header rather than send empty or raise — an empty correlation header pollutes the gateway, and raising would break standalone ops merely because headers are globally configured (observability must never break an operation). Asymmetry with unset-${env:VAR}-raises is deliberate and now stated: env absence is a config mistake, run absence is legitimate runtime context. Applied to 26ae + epic."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787715812195902001,"uuid":"7a6cb690-8308-4743-9cfb-7f318fb73005"}